Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: Get emergency medical help if you have signs of an allergic reaction to levothyroxine.
Signs of an allergic reaction to levothyroxine include hives, difficult breathing, and swelling of your face, lips, tongue, or throat.
Allergic reactions are usually caused by the inactive ingredients in a product rather than by levothyroxine itself.
Your doctor may suggest trying a different brand or form.
Levothyroxine may cause serious side effects.
Call your doctor at once if you have:
sudden pain or trouble moving your hip, wrist, or back;
fast or irregular heartbeats, or a pounding heartbeat;
chest pain, pain spreading to your jaw or shoulder;
wheezing or shortness of breath;
swelling in your legs or ankles, or new or worsening breathlessness when lying down;
fever, swollen glands, itching, joint pain, or not feeling well;
nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea;
confusion or feeling disoriented;
a seizure; or
high blood sugar - increased thirst, increased urination, dry mouth, fruity breath odor.
Common levothyroxine side effects may include:
fever, hot flashes, increased sweating, feeling too hot;
Triplet: ["levothyroxine", "has serious side effect symptom", "increased urination"]

The relation 'has serious side effect symptom' in the triplet is defined as 'An occurrence of the serious side effect specified by the subject drug may include the symptom specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
B. 'has serious side effect': The subject drug may cause the serious or potentially dangerous adverse effect specified by the object entity that requires medical attention.
C. 'has side effect frequency': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect specified by the object entity with the frequency indicated.
D. 'has overdose symptom': An overdose of the subject drug may cause the symptom specified by the object entity.
E. 'has side effect location': The adverse effect caused by the subject drug occurs at the location specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
